She's an amazing woman, your mother.


00:14:42.085 --> 00:14:45.500
- Yeah. Listen, Dr. -
- Marshall. Dr. Paige Marshall.


00:14:45.573 --> 00:14:47.482
Hi. She's getting worse.


00:14:47.556 --> 00:14:50.109
She-She never knows who I am anymore
and now she won't eat.


00:14:50.180 --> 00:14:53.147
- Even when the lawyer comes to visit?
- There's no lawyer.


00:14:53.220 --> 00:14:56.154
I'm the lawyer. Today she spat out
cannelloni from Cicero's.


00:14:56.228 --> 00:14:58.138
That's like her death row favorite meal.


00:14:58.211 --> 00:15:00.448
I've seen her sprint 10 blocks in heels
just to steal it.


00:15:00.516 --> 00:15:03.298
We're reaching the point
where decisions have to be made.


00:15:03.364 --> 00:15:05.502
Decisions?
What do you mean, decisions?


00:15:05.571 --> 00:15:07.710
Dr. Marshall.!


00:15:09.219 --> 00:15:11.739
- You'll have to excuse me now.
- Hey, hey.


00:15:11.810 --> 00:15:15.072
Could we go somewhere and talk,
you know, about my mother and stuff?


00:15:15.138 --> 00:15:17.407
- Now?
- Or later.


00:15:17.474 --> 00:15:20.409
We could meet for a drink
or, uh-you know.


00:15:20.482 --> 00:15:22.522
Are you asking me out?


00:15:22.594 --> 00:15:27.067
Well, no. Sort of. I mean, yeah.


00:15:27.138 --> 00:15:30.007
I have to finish my rounds now,
Mr. Mancini.


00:15:30.082 --> 00:15:32.318
We'll talk again on your next visit.


00:15:32.385 --> 00:15:34.873
But-


00:15:35.073 --> 00:15:38.334
- These are your grandparents, right?
- Um, I guess so, yeah.


00:15:38.401 --> 00:15:41.302
- I never met them.
- Why do they look like that?


00:15:41.376 --> 00:15:44.540
- They're Italian.
- Like, from Italy?


00:15:44.608 --> 00:15:46.844
Yeah.


00:15:46.912 --> 00:15:49.727
Uh, Mom came for boarding school
and never went back.


00:15:49.792 --> 00:15:52.181
Ah. Look at her here.


00:15:54.911 --> 00:15:58.260
Wow. She was really,
really, really, really-


00:15:58.335 --> 00:16:01.018
Hey, hey! What the fuck!


00:16:01.087 --> 00:16:03.901
- Dude.! That's my mom.
- I'm sorry, dude.


00:16:03.967 --> 00:16:06.355
- It's just, she was hot.
- No.


00:16:06.430 --> 00:16:10.358
Here. Make yourself useful.


00:16:10.430 --> 00:16:11.891
Man.


00:16:11.966 --> 00:16:14.235
"Dear Victor...


00:16:14.301 --> 00:16:16.538
"sorry to hear about your gums.


00:16:16.606 --> 00:16:18.428
"Hope this will help.


00:16:18.493 --> 00:16:20.664
Your pal, Bennett."


00:16:20.733 --> 00:16:23.635
- Who's Bennett?
- You met him. Sizzler on Western.


00:16:23.709 --> 00:16:26.491
Oh, yeah. Big guy?
Nearly broke a rib?


00:16:26.557 --> 00:16:28.891
That's him. How much?


00:16:28.956 --> 00:16:32.884
Uh, 32.


00:16:32.956 --> 00:16:35.639
Dollars? Thirty-two dollars?


00:16:35.708 --> 00:16:38.425
You know what $32 gets you
at a periodontist these days?


00:16:38.492 --> 00:16:40.826
- Why? What's wrong with your gums?
- Nothin'


00:16:40.892 --> 00:16:43.925
- I'm just saying, if there was.
- You're healthy.


00:16:43.996 --> 00:16:46.134
Let me explain something to you.
I provide a service.


00:16:46.203 --> 00:16:48.756
They send some cash.
It renews their savior experience.


00:16:48.827 --> 00:16:52.438
It's like when you adopt an overseas orphan,
only I'm right here.


00:16:52.506 --> 00:16:55.703
Besides, if I don't come up
with my monthly three grand...


00:16:55.771 --> 00:16:58.356
those vipers at St. Anthony's
won't let me in to feed her.


00:16:58.426 --> 00:17:00.117
- Fuck!
- What?


00:17:00.186 --> 00:17:01.615
I'm light.


00:17:01.690 --> 00:17:04.242
Again, Mr. Mancini?


00:17:04.314 --> 00:17:06.900
You're light again.


00:17:06.970 --> 00:17:09.042
Not to worry.


00:17:09.114 --> 00:17:14.296
I'm sure there's room
at the new state facility in Clancy.


00:17:14.361 --> 00:17:17.208
I hear they do a lovely porridge.


00:17:17.273 --> 00:17:19.574
Okay, okay, okay, okay.


00:17:20.985 --> 00:17:23.887
You got a pen?


00:17:28.823 --> 00:17:31.376
God bless you, Mr. Mancini.


00:17:38.615 --> 00:17:41.649
Come on.
It's eggplant parm from Gallini's.


00:17:41.719 --> 00:17:44.271
You love their eggplant. One bite.


00:17:44.342 --> 00:17:47.026
I'm not hungry.


00:17:47.095 --> 00:17:50.672
So, what are you doing? What's -
What's going on? Why are you-


00:17:50.742 --> 00:17:52.597
You're crying.


00:17:53.877 --> 00:17:56.812
What do you expect, Artie?
I'm dying.


00:17:56.886 --> 00:17:59.155
You're not dying. You're not dying.


00:17:59.222 --> 00:18:01.131
For Pete's sake, look at me.


00:18:01.205 --> 00:18:05.994
Half the time I don't even know
who I'm talking to anymore.


00:18:06.069 --> 00:18:08.752
Fine. Whatever.


00:18:08.821 --> 00:18:11.690
I've had enough
of this ridiculous planet.


00:18:14.260 --> 00:18:16.169
It's Victor.


00:18:17.875 --> 00:18:19.785
I can't bear it.


00:18:21.363 --> 00:18:24.908
- He has to know.
- Know what?


00:18:24.979 --> 00:18:26.921
Who he comes from.


00:18:26.995 --> 00:18:30.159
You said his father was a traveling salesman
from Norway with Tourette's.


00:18:30.227 --> 00:18:33.707
- I had to tell him something.
- You mean-You mean he's not?


00:18:33.779 --> 00:18:35.721
Of course he's not.


00:18:37.619 --> 00:18:40.553
You, uh-


00:18:40.626 --> 00:18:42.862
You have to tell him the truth, Ida.


00:18:42.930 --> 00:18:44.840
He's got a right to know.


00:18:44.913 --> 00:18:47.368
I've been trying for months now...


00:18:47.441 --> 00:18:52.176
but he so rarely comes to visit, and when
he does, I can't bring myself to say it.


00:18:52.241 --> 00:18:54.608
Listen to me now, Ida.


00:18:54.673 --> 00:18:57.672
It's very important that Victor
knows who he comes from...


00:18:57.744 --> 00:19:00.111
other than just, you know...


00:19:00.176 --> 00:19:02.031
you.


00:19:02.096 --> 00:19:04.103
- You really think so?
- Absolutely.


00:19:04.176 --> 00:19:07.045
Let me call him. I bet you
I could get him here lickety-split.


00:19:07.120 --> 00:19:09.673
- Oh, no. Oh, no, no, no, no. I
couldn't face that. No. - Well-


00:19:09.744 --> 00:19:13.322
You can tell me then.
I won't say a word.


00:19:13.392 --> 00:19:15.530
Attorney-client privilege and all.


00:19:15.599 --> 00:19:18.152
But, Artie, I really can't do that.


00:19:18.223 --> 00:19:20.078
Why not?


00:19:21.967 --> 00:19:25.447
'Cause I'm not even sure who you really are.


00:19:27.887 --> 00:19:31.018
Oh, I'm sorry, Artie.
I have to go.


00:19:32.397 --> 00:19:34.536
- Hey.
- Hi, Tito.


00:19:39.533 --> 00:19:42.184
Do you think she'll take you back?
She won't, you know.


00:19:42.253 --> 00:19:45.569
Pretty women
are narcissistic and unforgiving.


00:19:45.645 --> 00:19:47.499
You're pretty.


00:19:49.101 --> 00:19:52.199
I might have known.
You're too weak. You're too ordinary.


00:19:52.268 --> 00:19:54.985
This work requires vision.
It requires fortitude.


00:19:55.052 --> 00:19:57.157
What work?
You don't do any work.


00:19:57.228 --> 00:19:59.846
All you do is get in trouble.


00:19:59.916 --> 00:20:02.120
Don't you see? You are my work.


00:20:02.188 --> 00:20:04.577
All the political acts,
all the subversive happenings-


00:20:04.651 --> 00:20:06.658
They're all designed
to- to open your eyes.


00:20:06.731 --> 00:20:10.309
- Where's my father?
- Well, he's probably back in Oslo by now...


00:20:10.379 --> 00:20:13.794
offending his poor customers
with those unfortunate outbursts.


00:20:13.867 --> 00:20:16.038
I want to see him.


00:20:16.106 --> 00:20:19.455
He doesn't want you, Victor.
Why do you think he left?


00:20:22.474 --> 00:20:24.579
We need to talk.


00:20:24.650 --> 00:20:27.911
I think it's time we consider
a move to the second floor.


00:20:27.977 --> 00:20:31.076
The second floor?
No. Absolutely not.


00:20:31.146 --> 00:20:33.698
Mr. Mancini, your mother suffers
from a form of dementia...


00:20:33.769 --> 00:20:36.486
that's been exacerbated
by years of substance abuse.


00:20:36.553 --> 00:20:38.179
Dr. Fielding said it was Alzheimer's.


00:20:38.249 --> 00:20:41.827
There's a reason Dr. Fielding's
playing mini golf in Boca right now.


00:20:41.897 --> 00:20:43.806
Can we walk?


00:20:45.672 --> 00:20:47.614
Hey, did you try Aricept or Cognex?


00:20:47.688 --> 00:20:49.826
How would you know
about those drugs, Mr. Mancini?


00:20:49.896 --> 00:20:52.133
What about a glutamine blocker
like Memantine?


00:20:52.200 --> 00:20:55.876
We've tried everything. Once they've stopped
eating, the course is fairly predictable.


00:20:55.943 --> 00:20:58.627
Couldn't you force-feed her?
I'd be happy to help.


00:20:58.695 --> 00:21:00.669
I understand how you feel.


00:21:00.743 --> 00:21:04.485
Facing the possibility of a loved one's
demise can be very traumatic.


00:21:04.550 --> 00:21:08.325
Oh, no. I want her to die, just not
until I find out who my family is.


00:21:08.390 --> 00:21:11.259
Perhaps we should talk later
when you're not so upset.


00:21:11.334 --> 00:21:14.236
- You're absolutely right. What time do you get off?
- You don't have to do that.


00:21:14.310 --> 00:21:16.098
- What?
- Try to have sex with me.


00:21:16.166 --> 00:21:17.955
Oh, I really do.


00:21:18.022 --> 00:21:20.836
Well, I suppose that's flattering,
but I think we'd better not.


00:21:20.901 --> 00:21:25.341
- Why?
- Because you're just sad and lonely maybe.


00:21:25.413 --> 00:21:27.584
And you're realizing for the first time
that your mother...


00:21:27.653 --> 00:21:30.686
probably won't be getting better.


00:21:30.757 --> 00:21:33.691
And sleeping with me isn't gonna
change any of that, now, is it?


00:21:34.724 --> 00:21:36.546
Only one way to find out.


00:21:36.612 --> 00:21:38.434
Good night, Mr. Mancini.


00:21:40.260 --> 00:21:42.649
Hey.


00:21:42.724 --> 00:21:45.658
There's a little piece missing
from your ear.


00:21:45.731 --> 00:21:47.705
- I was clawed.
- Clawed?


00:21:47.779 --> 00:21:49.208
- By what?
- A lynx.


00:21:49.283 --> 00:21:50.744
- A lynx?
- It's like a bobcat.


00:21:50.819 --> 00:21:52.990
- I know what a lynx is.
- Oh.


00:21:55.138 --> 00:21:57.048
You lie a lot, huh?


00:21:57.122 --> 00:21:58.977
I guess.


00:22:07.617 --> 00:22:10.105
- You hurt me, Colin.
- Eva. I'm really not up to this.


00:22:10.177 --> 00:22:12.086
You touched me in my private place.


00:22:12.161 --> 00:22:13.884
Would you stop saying that?


00:22:13.953 --> 00:22:16.822
You said that it was just
a little game, a secret game...


00:22:16.896 --> 00:22:19.863
and then you put
your big man thing inside me!


00:22:19.936 --> 00:22:22.009
Okay, listen.


00:22:27.712 --> 00:22:29.915
Fine. You got me. I did it.


00:22:31.936 --> 00:22:34.302
- You admit it?
- Absolutely.


00:22:34.368 --> 00:22:38.197
I boned you silly.
Stuck it in every chance I got.


00:22:38.271 --> 00:22:42.045
After all these years,
you finally admit it!


00:22:42.110 --> 00:22:45.144
That's right. Now if you'll excuse me,
you got some pimento loaf in there.


00:22:45.215 --> 00:22:48.346
- It's not doing you any favors.
- And you're not sorry?


00:22:48.415 --> 00:22:50.935
Eva, baby, little sis,
of course I'm sorry.


00:22:51.006 --> 00:22:53.177
I was a wretched, disgusting horn dog.


00:22:53.246 --> 00:22:56.507
But you were such a hot tamale,
I couldn't control myself.


00:22:56.573 --> 00:22:58.962
Oh, look. Okay. Don't -


00:22:59.037 --> 00:23:01.426
Look, for Christ's sakes, don't do that.
Look, I'm sorry.


00:23:01.502 --> 00:23:04.818
I hurt your woo-woo,
but it was, like, 80 years ago.


00:23:04.892 --> 00:23:06.802
Can we please move on?


00:23:09.437 --> 00:23:11.292
Oh, Colin.


00:23:11.357 --> 00:23:13.691
Oh, Colin, I forgive you.


00:23:13.756 --> 00:23:15.861
I forgive you, Colin.


00:23:18.364 --> 00:23:21.211
- You can't nail your mom's doctor.
- Why not?


00:23:21.275 --> 00:23:23.926
'Cause later, when she hates you,
she might give her the wrong pills.


00:23:23.995 --> 00:23:27.061
Nah, she wouldn't do that. She took an oath.
Besides, now I have to fuck her.


00:23:27.131 --> 00:23:28.724
Why?


00:23:28.795 --> 00:23:31.282
Because she pinned me to the cork
like some stupid horny beetle specimen...


00:23:31.355 --> 00:23:33.210
without even breaking a sweat.


00:23:33.275 --> 00:23:35.413
And so now you want to
sleep with her for revenge?


00:23:35.482 --> 00:23:37.337
Yeah.


00:23:37.402 --> 00:23:41.046
I need her to keep my mom alive long enough
for me to get the truth out of her.


00:23:41.114 --> 00:23:43.667
Why? What do you think
you're gonna find out?


00:23:43.738 --> 00:23:46.488
That I come from somebody else too.
Somebody real. Somebody normal.


00:23:46.554 --> 00:23:50.710
After all the psychotic shit she put me
through, it's the least she can do, right?


00:23:50.777 --> 00:23:52.632
I'm supposed to lock him in, Victor.


00:23:52.697 --> 00:23:54.485
He was very specific about that.


00:23:54.553 --> 00:23:56.692
You touch these stocks,
you're goin' in, Norm...


00:23:56.761 --> 00:23:59.827
and you won't be wearin'
that nifty sentry getup either.


00:23:59.897 --> 00:24:02.002
Dick.


00:24:02.073 --> 00:24:03.927
You shouldn't have done that.


00:24:03.992 --> 00:24:07.341
Now Charlie's gonna lobby
the town council to banish us again.


00:24:07.416 --> 00:24:11.377
- So, what'd you do this time?
- Forgot to wash this off.


00:24:11.447 --> 00:24:15.702
You ever think you might be fuckin' up
on purpose just to keep yourself in here?


00:24:15.768 --> 00:24:19.859
Maybe. All this time in the stocks,
I got myself almost a week sober.


00:24:19.927 --> 00:24:22.065
I wouldn't get too carried away
with this whole sobriety thing.


00:24:22.135 --> 00:24:24.982
Given to what your body's used to,
you're liable to explode.


00:24:25.047 --> 00:24:27.861
How 'bout you?
You start your fourth step yet?


00:24:27.926 --> 00:24:29.836
That's the, um-


00:24:29.910 --> 00:24:32.692
That's the searching, fearless inventory
of everything you did...


00:24:32.758 --> 00:24:36.335
and was done to you
in your sordid sex addict history.


00:24:36.405 --> 00:24:39.820
If you need some help, I'd be happy
to remind you of heinous shit you did.


00:24:39.893 --> 00:24:41.748
Thanks. I'm good.


00:24:41.813 --> 00:24:43.668
Hey, wait a minute.


00:24:43.733 --> 00:24:46.286
If your mom already thinks...


00:24:46.357 --> 00:24:49.705
that you're Artie, or Fred,
or whoever...


00:24:49.780 --> 00:24:52.082
how are you gonna convince her
that you're really you?


00:24:52.149 --> 00:24:54.003
I'm not.


00:24:56.276 --> 00:25:01.065
- Hi. I'm Victor.
- Dude, don't -don't - Don't gild the lily, okay?


00:25:02.996 --> 00:25:05.134
- That's her?
- Yeah.


00:25:05.203 --> 00:25:07.854
She's young, for this place.


00:25:07.923 --> 00:25:10.443
- I know.
- And still kind of hot.


00:25:10.515 --> 00:25:12.620
Jesus!


00:25:12.691 --> 00:25:15.058
And she won't notice I'm not you?


00:25:15.123 --> 00:25:17.610
We're about to find out.


00:25:22.194 --> 00:25:25.991
Mrs. Mancini, I brought your son.
I brought Victor.


00:25:26.065 --> 00:25:27.920
No.


00:25:28.881 --> 00:25:31.815
- No. It's not.
- Yeah. Hi, Mom.


00:25:33.297 --> 00:25:35.817
It's Victor. Hi.


00:25:40.656 --> 00:25:42.511
Victor!


00:25:45.616 --> 00:25:47.721
- Is that really you?
- Yep.


00:25:47.792 --> 00:25:49.701
It really is.


00:25:52.560 --> 00:25:55.723
Oh, Victor.


00:25:55.791 --> 00:25:59.436
Mom, your hands are freezing.


00:25:59.503 --> 00:26:02.219
Dude?


00:26:02.287 --> 00:26:03.977
Oh, Victor.


00:26:05.006 --> 00:26:07.078
Hey, you know, in my experience...


00:26:07.150 --> 00:26:10.052
I have found
that these puzzles work best...


00:26:10.126 --> 00:26:12.777
if you find all the edge pieces first.


00:26:12.846 --> 00:26:15.180
Oh! Found a corner.


00:26:15.246 --> 00:26:18.890
Hey, wasn't there
something you were gonna tell him?


00:26:18.957 --> 00:26:20.812
- Huh?
- Wasn't there?


00:26:20.877 --> 00:26:23.178
Oh, yeah.


00:26:23.245 --> 00:26:25.666
I'm so happy you've come, Victor.


00:26:27.309 --> 00:26:30.821
I have so much to tell you.
I have so much to explain.


00:26:35.148 --> 00:26:37.450
Murray.


00:26:37.516 --> 00:26:39.850
This is between my son and I.


00:26:39.915 --> 00:26:42.785
- I think maybe I should stay here because-
- Go!


00:26:42.859 --> 00:26:46.088
- But you know, I don't think-
- Murray, please.


00:26:52.203 --> 00:26:54.853
My boy. My beautiful boy.


00:26:54.922 --> 00:26:57.671
- Are you Victor?
- Yeah.


00:26:57.739 --> 00:27:01.000
What'd l-What-What'd I do to you?


00:27:01.066 --> 00:27:02.921
Nothing.


00:27:05.962 --> 00:27:08.995
I'm so scared.


00:27:19.753 --> 00:27:24.127
That ceiling
was once covered with angels...


00:27:24.200 --> 00:27:26.110
but they painted over them.


00:27:26.184 --> 00:27:29.959
- Some papal decree.
- Vatican II.


00:27:31.080 --> 00:27:34.080
- Are you Catholic?
- My mom, she's from-


00:27:34.151 --> 00:27:36.672
Italy. I know.


00:27:40.615 --> 00:27:42.786
I think I've found a way to save her.


00:27:44.263 --> 00:27:47.645
But it's going to require
your participation.


00:27:47.718 --> 00:27:51.362
It's an experimental procedure.
It's illegal.


00:27:51.430 --> 00:27:53.502
I can't even guarantee it will work.


00:27:53.574 --> 00:27:55.778
In order to attempt this procedure...


00:27:55.846 --> 00:27:58.050
I'm going to need some embryonic tissue.


00:27:58.118 --> 00:28:00.867
Okay. Ho-Hold on a second.


00:28:00.933 --> 00:28:04.511
It's difficult for me to be so direct,
but time is a factor.


00:28:04.581 --> 00:28:07.745
My mucosa's so thick,
you could stand a spoon in it.


00:28:07.813 --> 00:28:09.788
Are you fucking with me?


00:28:09.860 --> 00:28:12.446
Given the options available to us,
this is her only hope.


00:28:12.517 --> 00:28:15.713
The good news is
she's an ideal candidate.


00:28:15.780 --> 00:28:19.358
All she needs is a healthy,
genetically compatible donor.


00:28:19.428 --> 00:28:21.402
And-And you know what to do?


00:28:21.475 --> 00:28:24.442
I put myself through med school
working nights in a stem cell research lab.


00:28:24.515 --> 00:28:29.087
That's hot. But why-why would you
put yourself out like this for her?


00:28:29.155 --> 00:28:31.872
Your mother
has been an inspiration to me.


00:28:31.939 --> 00:28:33.946
She changed my life.


00:28:34.019 --> 00:28:38.274
I'd never be able to forgive myself
if I didn't do everything I could to save her.


00:28:38.339 --> 00:28:40.760
Are we talking about the same person?


